{"resourceIdentifier":"3980","resourceName":"Xinjiang Muge Swine Farm Manure Management System GHG Mitigation Project","description":"Xinjiang Muge Swine Farm Manure Management System GHG Mitigation Project (hereafter referred to as the project) introduces new animal waste management systems (AWMSs) to treat the manure from 3 existing swine farms in  Xinjiang Province, which are owned by AKSU Xingjiang MUGE food Co., Ltd. The purpose of the project activity is to treat the manure and wastewater to avoid methane emissions generated in the baseline uncovered anaerobic lagoons. \r\nIn this project, AWMS is built to replace the traditional open anaerobic lagoons, and each subsidiary swine farm installed one AWMS. The manure and waster will be collected into the anaerobic digesters and then biogas generated during the anaerobic treatment process will be captured and total of 3.7 million m3 biogas is expected to be generated annually. Biogas is then sent into biogas boilers for heat production. Every biogas boiler has been installed in each swine farm. All of the heat generated is used by AWMSs and the swine farms, while the rest (if any) will be burned. The sludge produced after fermentation is applied to cornfields as fertilizer, and the wastewater produced by anaerobic biogas digesters is used for agricultural irrigation.\r\nBenefiting from the “waste-biogas-fertilizer” pattern, harmlessness and ecological utilization of the swine manure can be realized. All the heat generated by the project will be used by the AWMSs and 3 swine farms. The heat generated will not be connected to other users or the regional heating supply system and the baseline emissions associated with heat generation will not be claimed. The project activity will reduce GHG in the atmosphere by avoiding methane emissions from anaerobic treatment of swine manure and wastewater. The project is expected to achieve an annual emission reduction of 415,544 tCO2e and a total emission reduction of 2,908,811 tCO2e in the first crediting period.","location":{"latitude":81.782955,"longitude":40.632294},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2023-01-10","endExclusive":"2023-02-10","endInclusive":"2023-02-09"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"3980"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Aksu City Xinjiang (Uygur Autonomous Region)"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Aksu Xingjiang Muge FOOD Co., Ltd."},{"type":"string","value":"Xinjiang Uyghur Autonomous Region, China"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"3980"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"165560"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Livestock, enteric fermentation, and manure management"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"ACM0010"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"CTI Certification Co., Ltd."}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"16/07/2024"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1st, 30/08/2021 - 29/08/2028"}]}]}],"documentGroups":[{"code":"VCS_PIPELINE_DOCUMENTS","description":"VCS Pipeline Documents","documents":[{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=82394&IDKEY=a98klasmf8jflkasf8098afnasfkj98f0a9sfsakjflsakjf8ds113621326","documentType":"Draft Project Description","documentName":"VCS_PROJ_DESC_PCP_3980_29NOV2022.pdf","uploadDate":"2023-01-10T17:59:01.427Z"},{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=79706&IDKEY=n097809fdslkjf09rndasfufd098asodfjlkduf09nm23mrn87f109914574","documentType":"Listing Representation","documentName":"VCS-Listing-Representatio